   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "Approach to the man with genital symptoms not needing urgent attention • First assess and advise the man with genital symptoms 62. Test for HIV 124. If HIV positive, give routine care 126. If negative, repeat in 6 weeks. Consider need for PrEP 119. • Check for urethral discharge: if no visible discharge, ask patient to milk the urethra. If no urethral discharge and urinary symptoms (burning/frequency/urgency) 69",
